{"tool_name":"lead-or","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"lead-or","home":"https://www.lead-dbs.org","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A multimodal platform for deep brain stimulation surgery.","addition_date":"2022-08-28T21:12:25.169193Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:46:12.349521Z","tool_type":["Library","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:lead-or","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"simon.oxenford@charite.de","name":"Sim\u00f3n Oxenford","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2989-3861","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Andreas Horn","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0695-6025"},{"name":"Jan Roediger","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2814-3532"},{"name":"Luka Milosevic","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4051-5397"},{"name":"Wolf-Julian Neumann","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6758-9708"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"},{"term":"Trajectory visualization","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3890"}]}],"name":"Lead-OR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.7554/elife.72929","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) electrode implant trajectories are stereotactically defined using preoperative neuroimaging. To validate the correct trajectory, microelectrode recordings (MER) or local field potential recordings (LFP) can be used to extend neuroanatomical information (defined by magnetic resonance imaging) with neurophysiological activity patterns recorded from micro-and macroelectrodes probing the surgical target site. Currently, these two sources of information (imaging vs. electrophysiology) are analyzed separately, while means to fuse both data streams have not been introduced. Methods: Here we present a tool that integrates resources from stereotactic planning, neuroimaging, MER and high-resolution atlas data to create a real-time visualization of the implant trajectory. We validate the tool based on a retrospective cohort of DBS patients (N = 52) offline and present single use cases of the real-time platform. Results: We establish an open-source software tool for multimodal data visualization and analysis during DBS surgery. We show a general correspondence between features derived from neuroimaging and electrophysiological recordings and present examples that demonstrate the functionality of the tool. Conclusions: This novel software platform for multimodal data visualization and analysis bears translational potential to improve accuracy of DBS surgery. The toolbox is made openly available and is extendable to integrate with additional software packages.","authors":[{"name":"Guttler C."},{"name":"Horn A."},{"name":"Kuhn A."},{"name":"Milosevic L."},{"name":"Neudorfer C."},{"name":"Neumann W.-J."},{"name":"Oxenford S."},{"name":"Roediger J."},{"name":"Spindler P."},{"name":"Vajkoczy P."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2022-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"eLife","title":"Lead-OR: A Multimodal Platform for Deep Brain Stimulation Surgery"},"pmcid":"PMC9177150","pmid":"35594135"}],"topic":[{"term":"MRI","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3444"},{"term":"Medical imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3384"},{"term":"Neurobiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3304"},{"term":"Physiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3300"},{"term":"Surgery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3421"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Lead-OR","home":"https://bio.tools/lead-or","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A multimodal platform for deep brain stimulation surgery.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:lead-or/lib/www.lead-dbs.org","@license":"https://creativecommons